WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.461
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.020
Robots are what I do.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.090
I like to build robots.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.560
I like to program them.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:21.220
To me, a robot is
something that's a machine,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.450
and it somehow senses the world.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:26.530
And then it computes, thinks
about what the sensors tell it,

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.790
and then it acts in the world.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.530
For a number of years,
building robots [INAUDIBLE]

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.623
unstructured environments.

00:00:43.623 --> 00:00:45.790
We've been building them
with three different levels

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.970
of control.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:51.600
The primitive level, where the
motors and sensors operate.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.580
A skills level, where
they have basic skills.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.650
A behavior level, which
gives them behaviors

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.710
like going through
a mountain pass,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.180
finding some dirt on the
floor to clean up, et cetera.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.490
No.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.410
No.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.230
You're not to do that.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:29.730
No.

00:01:32.694 --> 00:01:35.420
Not appropriate.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.830
No.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.700
We are a mechanism.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.540
If we are machines, then
in principle at least,

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.270
we should be able to
build machines out

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:50.130
of other stuff, which are
just as alive as we are.

00:01:52.497 --> 00:01:54.830
So trying to make robots that
are safe to interact with,

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:58.660
so that ultimately doing stuff
with us and partnering with us,

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.630
is going to be important
in our old age.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.500
We have to have more
robotics help and assistance.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.560
We're not there yet,
but I think we're making

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.250
good progress towards it.

